n, Isha publishes the verified hazards and uncertainties to all sides instead of endorsing either faction. She ends willing to accept responsibility for the consequences of sharing imperfect knowledge rather than letting silence decide who gets access.","personality_traits":["observant","cautious","methodical","quietly brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift cartography","description":"Can chart shifting skybridge routes and identify how island drift and wind currents affect safe passage.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Record verification","description":"Can compare route logs, maintenance notes, and toll ledgers to expose discrepancies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_toma_rell","name":"Toma Rell","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Toma Rell is a miller and grain steward on The Hollow, where windmills turn the harvest into food for much of the archipelago. He learned during the Great Calm's inherited stories that a settlement must be able to feed itself, but he also knows that isolation has a cost. Toma is tall and spare, with flour caught in the seams of his sleeves and a weathered face that rarely reveals how much he has already calculated.","motivation":"Keep the people of The Hollow fed without allowing the Drift Cartel to use grain as leverage.","goal":"Arrange fair grain deliveries to the isolated seventh ring and other settlements without accepting a Cartel levy that would weaken the Circle's independence.","flaw":"He guards supplies so tightly that he can mistake caution for fairness.","internal_conflict":"Toma believes self-reliance is essential, yet withholding grain from others would repeat the abandonment that made the Great Calm so damaging.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy strains the Hollow Circle's control of its harvest, while the seventh ring's isolation threatens residents who depend on deliveries.","arc":"Toma begins by refusing to release grain until the Cartel lev