[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Mara Voss is a cloudstone cable engineer raised among the shielded forge-pits of Emberroost. She became known for finding faults in bridge braids before they failed, and for believing that every connection can be repaired if someone is willing to take responsibility for it. Now responsible for maintaining the elevator links between the ship's habitable rings, she is caught between her Warden oath and the seventh ring's declaration of independence. She is broad-shouldered, with close-cropped dark hair, a scarred left hand, and copper wire tucked into the cuff of her work coat.","motivation":"Keep people on every ring supplied and connected without letting the Bridge Wardens become an instrument of coercion.","goal":"Find a way to restore safe passage between the seventh ring and the other tiers after its elevators are severed.","flaw":"She treats technical problems as if they can be solved without confronting who has the power to choose.","internal_conflict":"Mara's Warden oath tells her to preserve the network, but she fears that restoring it by force would make the bridges she protects symbols of domination.","external_conflict":"The severed elevators isolate residents, while the Bridge Wardens and Drift Cartel dispute responsibility for access, tolls, and repairs.","arc":"Mara begins determined to reconnect the tiers first and debate politics later. When the Drift Cartel demands that she reopen the elevator links under its toll authority, she refuses and offers the seventh ring a role in deciding the terms of safe passage. By the end, she still works to repair connections, but no longer assumes that engineering alone gives her the right to decide who uses them.","personality_traits":["precise","steadfast","reserved","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable diagnosis","description":"Can identify strain and braid failures in cloudstone skybridge cables through close inspection and practical testing.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Emergency rigging","description":"Can improvise a temporary, load-limited crossing when a maintained route is damaged, while accounting for wind-debt obligations.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_kael","name":"Ren Kael","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Ren Kael is a senior route broker for the Drift Cartel, born into the crowded ledgers and shifting shipping schedules of Mistral Docks. He rose by making trade dependable when wind currents and island drift made promises difficult to keep. He sees the seventh ring's independence declaration as a threat to the routes that feed the archipelago, and treats centralized control as the price of preventing another age of isolation. Ren is lean and immaculate, with silvered hair combed back and a dark ledger case chained to his wrist.","motivation":"Preserve the inter-isle trade system that he believes keeps the archipelago from becoming vulnerable and divided.","goal":"Bring the seventh ring's elevator access under a Cartel agreement before the severance disrupts shipping and trade.","flaw":"He confuses control with stability and assumes that people will accept coercion if it keeps goods moving.","internal_conflict":"Ren fears a return to the self-reliance and isolation taught by the Great Calm, yet his methods risk creating the very separation he wants to prevent.","external_conflict":"The seventh ring rejects Cartel authority, while the Bridge Wardens resist letting merchants dictate access to the elevator system.","arc":"Ren begins certain that the Cartel must take control of the severed elevator links to keep trade alive. When his attempt to impose toll terms causes the Hollow Circle to withhold grain shipments, he must choose between escalation and negotiating access without a Cartel monopoly. He ends the story accepting shared oversight, though he remains wary that cooperation may fail.","personality_traits":["calculating","persuasive","anxious","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route bargaining","description":"Can negotiate shipping schedules and exchange terms among merchants who depend on the drifting routes.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade forecasting","description":"Can track how tolls, wind conditions, and disrupted links are likely to affect the flow of goods.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_isha_tenn","name":"Isha Tenn","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Isha Tenn is a cartographer and records keeper at Silverspine Academy, where she charts how the skybridge network shifts with the islands and their currents. She joined the Bridge Wardens to make their maintenance decisions accountable, but her maps have also become valuable to anyone seeking leverage over a route. Isha is small and quick-moving, with ink-stained fingertips, a pale green scarf, and a roll of annotated charts always strapped across her back.","motivation":"Make decisions about access and safety depend on accurate maps rather than political claims.","goal":"Document which routes and elevator connections can be safely restored without concealing the risks from the people who will use them.","flaw":"She hides behind precise records when a decision requires her to take a public position.","internal_conflict":"Isha wants her knowledge to protect people, but fears that making it public will let one faction use it to dominate the others.","external_conflict":"The severed elevator network has left conflicting claims about safe routes, and both the Cartel and Wardens want her charts to support their plans.","arc":"Isha begins by withholding her complete route charts until she can verify every detail. When Ren demands a map to justify Cartel control and Mara asks her to help assess a shared repair plan, Isha publishes the verified hazards and uncertainties to all sides instead of endorsing either faction. She ends willing to accept responsibility for the consequences of sharing imperfect knowledge rather than letting silence decide who gets access.","personality_traits":["observant","cautious","methodical","quietly brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift cartography","description":"Can chart shifting skybridge routes and identify how island drift and wind currents affect safe passage.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Record verification","description":"Can compare route logs, maintenance notes, and toll ledgers to expose discrepancies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_toma_rell","name":"Toma Rell","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Toma Rell is a miller and grain steward on The Hollow, where windmills turn the harvest into food for much of the archipelago. He learned during the Great Calm's inherited stories that a settlement must be able to feed itself, but he also knows that isolation has a cost. Toma is tall and spare, with flour caught in the seams of his sleeves and a weathered face that rarely reveals how much he has already calculated.","motivation":"Keep the people of The Hollow fed without allowing the Drift Cartel to use grain as leverage.","goal":"Arrange fair grain deliveries to the isolated seventh ring and other settlements without accepting a Cartel levy that would weaken the Circle's independence.","flaw":"He guards supplies so tightly that he can mistake caution for fairness.","internal_conflict":"Toma believes self-reliance is essential, yet withholding grain from others would repeat the abandonment that made the Great Calm so damaging.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy strains the Hollow Circle's control of its harvest, while the seventh ring's isolation threatens residents who depend on deliveries.","arc":"Toma begins by refusing to release grain until the Cartel levy is withdrawn, convinced that any concession will invite further demands. When the severed elevators leave the seventh ring short of supplies, he commits a measured reserve to a shared delivery plan negotiated with Mara and the Circle, rather than waiting for a perfect settlement. He ends prepared to share responsibility for food security without surrendering the Hollow's right to set fair terms.","personality_traits":["patient","prudent","stubborn","compassionate"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain stewardship","description":"Can estimate harvest reserves and plan measured distributions without undermining future supplies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Mill maintenance","description":"Can keep windmills operating through routine repairs and careful adjustment to changing currents.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ren_kael","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Voss and Ren Kael clash over the severed elevator links: Mara insists safe repairs must not become Cartel control, while Ren sees her refusal as a threat to the trade routes he manages."},{"id":"rel_ren_isha","source_character_id":"chr_ren_kael","target_character_id":"chr_isha_tenn","relationship_type":"pressure","description":"Ren Kael pressures Isha Tenn to provide charts that support Cartel authority; Isha's insistence on publishing hazards and uncertainty undermines his preferred account of the routes."},{"id":"rel_toma_mara","source_character_id":"chr_toma_rell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Toma Rell allies with Mara Voss to organize a fair supply route for isolated residents, but challenges her whenever engineering priorities overlook the food needed to sustain people."},{"id":"rel_isha_mara","source_character_id":"chr_isha_tenn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"colleague","description":"Isha Tenn provides Mara Voss with verified route assessments, while Mara's repair plans force Isha to make her careful research useful under pressure."}]}
</Output>
