description":"Finds discrepancies in toll accounts and cargo manifests, tracing patterns across many small transactions.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Quiet negotiation","description":"Can keep a tense discussion civil long enough to learn what each side fears losing.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_tallis","name":"Oren Tallis","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Oren Tallis is a senior Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, where he learned to judge a bridge by its tension, its repairs, and the workers who maintain it. His years inspecting cloudstone cables have left his hands scarred and his coat patched with practical reinforcements. Oren once approved a Cartel-financed repair contract to keep several crossings open; he now suspects that its hidden costs helped fund the cathedral relic trade. He is patient with machinery and blunt with people, especially those who confuse safety with obedience.","motivation":"Keep the skybridge network safe without allowing its maintenance to become a pretext for extortion.","goal":"Expose the unsafe and corrupt terms of the Cartel's repair contract before another crossing is compromised.","flaw":"He takes too much responsibility on himself and hides mistakes to protect the people who trusted his judgment.","internal_conflict":"Oren believes engineers must own the consequences of their decisions, yet fears that admitting his approval helped the Cartel will discredit the Wardens he serves.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel controls the funds and shipping access needed for repairs, and disclosure of the contract could intensify the Toll War and leave bridges vulnerable.","arc":"Oren begins by quietly trying to correct the contract's damage without revealing his part in it. When a threatened crossing forces him to choose between a concealed patch and a public warning that may halt traffic, he reports the danger and admits he approved the original terms. He ends as a more candid Warden, willing to share responsibility and demand safer conditions openly.","personality_traits":["methodical","protective","stubborn","plainspoken"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable assessment","description":"Recognizes strain, faulty braiding, and dangerous repairs through close inspection of cloudstone bridgework.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Crew leadership","description":"Organizes repair crews calmly during hazardous work and makes sure each person understands the risks.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sera_holm","name":"Sera Holm","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Sera Holm is a Hollow Circle grain broker who grew up measuring each season by the mill's stores and the wind that carried them to market. During the Great Calm, her grandparents' accounts became a family record of how quickly distant allies could become unreachable. Sera is broad-shouldered, with flour caught in the seams of her dark clothes and a simple windmill pin at her collar. She has used Cartel contracts to secure grain shipments for the Hollow, but now intends to control the cathedral relic trade's proceeds as leverage against the Cartel's grain levy. Her protective purpose has hardened into a willingness to make others bear the cost.","motivation":"Ensure the Hollow Circle can feed its people without submitting to a Cartel levy.","goal":"Use the secret cathedral trade to force the Cartel to withdraw its claim on Hollow grain shipments.","flaw":"She mistakes coercion for protection and assumes that only she can decide which risks her community should take.","internal_conflict":"Sera despises the Cartel for treating food as a bargaining chip, but her own scheme makes the Hollow's survival depend on another hidden bargain.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens the Hollow Circle, while Sera's secret dealings put her at odds with Mara's evidence and could provoke retaliation against the island's food supply.","arc":"Sera begins certain that secret leverage is the only language the Cartel understands. When Mara's evidence reveals that the cathedral trade could let merchants tighten their grip on grain rather than release it, Sera must choose between seizing the proceeds alone or publicly joining the Hollow Circle's resistance. She ends by abandoning the coercive bargain and accepting a collective, riskier stand against the levy.","personality_traits":["determined","practical","protective","calculating"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain logistics","description":"Can estimate stores, shipment needs, and how a delay or levy will affect the Hollow's food supply.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bargaining","description":"Understands the pressure points in trade agreements and can make a difficult offer sound like the other party's best option.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_oren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_oren_tallis","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara needs Oren to verify the bridge-repair records tied to her ledger, while Oren distrusts her secrecy and fears she will expose the Wardens without regard for the crossings they maintain."},{"id":"rel_sera_mara","source_character_id":"chr_sera_holm","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sera sees Mara's investigation as a threat to the leverage she needs against the Cartel; Mara sees Sera's secret bargain as a danger to the Hollow Circle and the truth."},{"id":"rel_sera_oren","source_character_id":"chr_sera_holm","target_character_id":"chr_oren_tallis","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Sera distrusts Oren because the Wardens' repairs can keep Cartel-controlled trade moving, while Oren believes Sera's willingness to gamble with hidden deals could make both food shipments and bridges less safe."}]}
