{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Mara Voss is a Bridge Warden marshal from Emberroost, raised among the forge-pits where cloudstone cables are braided and inspected. Broad-shouldered and weathered, she wears a patched Warden coat, keeps her dark hair cropped close, and carries a ledger of crossing debts beside her tools. Years spent enforcing bridge safety have made her exacting; she once allowed a Cartel shipment through during a dangerous wind shift and has never forgiven herself for the workers injured afterward.","motivation":"Keep the skybridges and the people who depend on them safe, while making amends for the harm caused by her past leniency.","goal":"Stop the stolen locomotive before it reaches the Hollow and exposes the Circle's grain shipments to the Cartel's control.","flaw":"She treats rules as a substitute for judgment and struggles to trust anyone who bends them.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that any compromise will repeat her earlier failure, even when rigid enforcement could endanger others.","external_conflict":"A Drift Cartel prince has stolen a cloudstone locomotive and is using it to seize control of the skybridge route and impose a grain levy; Mara must stop him without causing a bridge failure or ignoring wind-debt obligations.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that the Warden code alone can prevent disaster. When the locomotive threatens a skybridge and the Cartel's toll collectors demand immediate repayment of crossing wind-debt, she chooses to trust Sella's improvised diversion instead of pursuing a technically lawful but dangerous interception. By the end, she still protects the rules that keep people safe, but accepts that sound judgment sometimes requires adapting them with others."},{"id":"chr_sella_quill","name":"Sella Quill","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Sella Quill grew up around the cargo ledgers and shifting bargains of Mistral Docks, where she learned to pass as a clerk, courier, or harmless passenger whenever it suited her. Slender, quick-eyed, and dressed in a travel coat with too many hidden pockets, she can read a shipping manifest as readily as a room full of suspicious merchants. She once worked for the Drift Cartel and knows the stolen locomotive's paperwork, but her talent for escape has left her with few allies and a reputation she cannot simply talk her way out of.","motivation":"Prove she can use her talent for deception to protect people rather than merely save herself.","goal":"Help Mara take the locomotive away from the Cartel prince before he uses it to dominate grain shipments from the Hollow.","flaw":"She lies reflexively and hoards information, believing that dependence on anyone is a trap.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to be trusted but fears that telling the truth will leave her powerless and exposed.","external_conflict":"The Cartel knows Sella helped steal the locomotive and is hunting her, while the route's crossing debts and Warden inspections make it difficult to hide or redirect the train.","arc":"Sella begins treating every alliance as a temporary con and keeps the locomotive's route plans to herself. When the Cartel prince uses a false manifest to endanger the Hollow's grain shipment, she publicly gives Mara the real route and admits her own role in the theft, sacrificing her best cover to prevent the seizure. She ends the chase still clever and wary, but willing to share the truth and accept accountability."},{"id":"chr_orlan_kest","name":"Orlan Kest","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Orlan Kest is a powerful Drift Cartel merchant prince based at Mistral Docks, accustomed to turning shipping access into political leverage. Immaculately dressed in dark, salt-stiffened finery, he wears a brass route-token from the Cartel Charter and carries himself like a man who believes every obligation can be priced. He acquired influence by promising reliable trade after the Great Calm, but now treats the archipelago's dependence on moving goods as proof that he should control its bridges and harvests.","motivation":"Secure lasting power over inter-isle trade by making the Cartel indispensable to every settlement.","goal":"Use the stolen locomotive to control the skybridge route and force the Hollow Circle to accept the Cartel's grain levy.","flaw":"He mistakes dependence for loyalty and assumes everyone has a price.","internal_conflict":"Orlan fears that without control over trade he will lose the authority that has defined his identity, so he cannot distinguish respect from submission.","external_conflict":"Mara's Warden authority and Sella's knowledge of his route records threaten his attempt to seize the locomotive's route, while the Hollow Circle resists his levy and the Toll War weakens his grip on trade.","arc":"Orlan begins certain that wealth and control can make every rival comply. When Sella reveals the true route and Mara refuses to let his train cross a vulnerable bridge, he has the chance to abandon the seizure and preserve safe passage, but instead orders the locomotive onward and loses the cooperation he needs. By the end, his plan is broken and the Cartel's merchants begin questioning him; he must face that coercion has made his power brittle rather than secure."}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_sella","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara Voss needs Sella Quill's knowledge of the stolen locomotive and Cartel routes, but Sella's history of deception makes Mara question whether she is being helped or manipulated."},{"id":"rel_sella_orlan","source_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","target_character_id":"chr_orlan_kest","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sella Quill once worked for Orlan Kest and knows how he turns shipping records into leverage; Orlan sees her betrayal as a threat to his control of the locomotive and the Cartel's route plans."},{"id":"rel_mara_orlan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_orlan_kest","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Voss is sworn to protect the skybridges that Orlan Kest wants to control, putting her safety-first Warden duty directly against his attempt to force the Hollow Circle into the grain levy."}]}
