"name":"Fleet command","description":"Coordinates sail-driven vessels through close formations and dangerous bridge passages.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_cael_vel","name":"Cael Vel","role":"antagonist","description":"Cael Vel is Mara's estranged elder brother and an admiral whose fleet enforces the Drift Cartel's grip on the shipping lanes. He once trained beside Mara in the currents around Mistral Docks, but left after concluding that the Bridge Wardens' safety obligations gave merchants too much power to delay trade. Cael is tall and composed, with silver threaded through his dark hair and a formal coat marked by salt and wind. He insists that every order is a calculation, though he remembers every name lost to the Great Calm.","motivation":"Prevent another age of isolation by keeping the archipelago's trade moving, even at the cost of coercion.","goal":"Force the Wardens to accept the Cartel's toll system and reopen the lanes under Cartel authority.","flaw":"He mistakes decisive control for stability and dismisses the human cost of enforcing it.","internal_conflict":"Cael still loves Mara and fears that admitting the Cartel's methods are wrong would mean admitting his years of service have deepened the very divisions he meant to prevent.","external_conflict":"Mara's fleet and the Bridge Wardens resist his blockade, while the Hollow Circle's grain shipments make his control of the lanes increasingly unpopular.","arc":"Cael begins certain that pressure is the only language the Wardens understand. When Mara's fleet refuses an easy engagement and a delayed grain convoy puts the Hollow Circle at risk, he must choose between tightening the blockade or allowing a guarded passage. He opens the route under terms that expose his disagreement with the Cartel, ending as a rival still responsible for his choices rather than an unquestioning instrument of control.","personality_traits":["strategic"