{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vel","name":"Mara Vel","role":"protagonist","description":"Mara Vel is a fleet officer raised among the wind-battered moorings of Mistral Docks. She earned her commission by learning to read gusts, currents, and shifting bridge approaches with more patience than bravado. Her brother, Cael, left home after a bitter dispute over the Drift Cartel's control of shipping lanes; years later, he became an admiral on the opposing side. Mara is spare in speech and posture, with close-cropped dark hair, a weather-lined face, and a brass compass worn smooth by her thumb.","motivation":"Keep the skybridge network and the settlements that depend on it from being sacrificed to the Toll War.","goal":"Lead her fleet to stop Cael's blockade of the bridges without severing the routes that carry food and trade between the isles.","flaw":"She treats restraint as a private burden and withholds information from her crew, believing that command means carrying every uncertainty alone.","internal_conflict":"Mara must decide whether loyalty to her duty requires her to oppose her brother openly, or whether family gives her reason to risk the fleet's safety for him.","external_conflict":"Her fleet faces Cael's superior blockade tactics, while the Cartel's tolls and the Wardens' demand for safe crossings leave little room for a clean victory.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that a commander must conceal doubt to keep others steady. When Cael's blockade threatens a bridge crossing whose wind-debt is already due, she tells her officers the full risks and asks them to help choose a route. By the end, she still confronts Cael as an enemy admiral, but leads through shared judgment rather than solitary control.","personality_traits":["stoic","observant","disciplined","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Current reading","description":"Judges shifting wind currents and uses them to guide a fleet through drifting-isle approaches.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Fleet command","description":"Coordinates sail-driven vessels through close formations and dangerous bridge passages.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_cael_vel","name":"Cael Vel","role":"antagonist","description":"Cael Vel is Mara's estranged elder brother and an admiral whose fleet enforces the Drift Cartel's grip on the shipping lanes. He once trained beside Mara in the currents around Mistral Docks, but left after concluding that the Bridge Wardens' safety obligations gave merchants too much power to delay trade. Cael is tall and composed, with silver threaded through his dark hair and a formal coat marked by salt and wind. He insists that every order is a calculation, though he remembers every name lost to the Great Calm.","motivation":"Prevent another age of isolation by keeping the archipelago's trade moving, even at the cost of coercion.","goal":"Force the Wardens to accept the Cartel's toll system and reopen the lanes under Cartel authority.","flaw":"He mistakes decisive control for stability and dismisses the human cost of enforcing it.","internal_conflict":"Cael still loves Mara and fears that admitting the Cartel's methods are wrong would mean admitting his years of service have deepened the very divisions he meant to prevent.","external_conflict":"Mara's fleet and the Bridge Wardens resist his blockade, while the Hollow Circle's grain shipments make his control of the lanes increasingly unpopular.","arc":"Cael begins certain that pressure is the only language the Wardens understand. When Mara's fleet refuses an easy engagement and a delayed grain convoy puts the Hollow Circle at risk, he must choose between tightening the blockade or allowing a guarded passage. He opens the route under terms that expose his disagreement with the Cartel, ending as a rival still responsible for his choices rather than an unquestioning instrument of control.","personality_traits":["strategic","formal","unyielding","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Blockade planning","description":"Positions sail-driven vessels to control approaches without relying on gunpowder.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Uses careful, measured bargains to secure compliance from merchants and officers.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_olin_rusk","name":"Olin Rusk","role":"supporting","description":"Olin Rusk is a Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, where he learned to inspect and repair the cloudstone cables that bind the drifting isles. Assigned to advise Mara's fleet, he knows that a ship's safest route may still impose a wind-debt that must be repaid in labour or goods within a season. He is broad-shouldered, with burnished skin, a neatly tied braid, and hands marked by years of cable work. He speaks plainly and trusts measurements more than promises.","motivation":"Keep the skybridges intact and ensure their maintenance is not treated as an invisible cost of commerce.","goal":"Secure a crossing plan that protects the bridges and accounts for the crew labour owed under the wind-debt rule.","flaw":"He clings to procedure even when urgent circumstances require him to trust people beyond the written measurements.","internal_conflict":"Olin fears that improvisation will turn one mistake into a catastrophe, but knows that rigid adherence to procedure can also leave people stranded.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pressures him to approve crossings faster than the Wardens can inspect them, while Mara's fleet needs an immediate route around Cael's blockade.","arc":"Olin begins insisting that no fleet cross until every cable and debt is accounted for. When Cael's blockade threatens a bridge approach and the crew faces a choice between delay and a measured but untested passage, Olin shares his calculations and lets Mara's officers adapt them in the moment. He ends still exacting about safety, but willing to combine procedure with the judgment of those who must act.","personality_traits":["methodical","direct","patient","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable inspection","description":"Identifies stress and wear in cloudstone bridge cables before they become dangerous.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Debt accounting","description":"Tracks the labour or goods owed for skybridge crossings within the season.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_cael","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_cael_vel","relationship_type":"estranged siblings","description":"Mara Vel and Cael Vel are estranged siblings whose opposing fleet commands turn old family loyalty into a direct conflict during the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_cael_mara","source_character_id":"chr_cael_vel","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Cael Vel sees Mara Vel as both his most perceptive rival and the one opponent whose judgment could make him question the Cartel's blockade."},{"id":"rel_olin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_olin_rusk","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Olin Rusk advises Mara Vel on bridge safety and wind-debt, challenging her to include her crew in decisions that affect their survival."}]}
