{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_tavi","name":"Tavi","role":"protagonist","description":"Tavi is a curious child from the Hollow, with wind-tangled dark curls, a patched yellow coat, and pockets full of odd buttons collected from passing traders. While hiding from a grain tally, Tavi discovers a small door that opens onto the same place yesterday. Tavi has always been proud of solving problems alone, especially when the adults seem too busy arguing over the Grain Levy to listen.","motivation":"Keep the Hollow's grain from being swallowed by the Cartel's levy.","goal":"Use the door to yesterday to find proof that the grain tally is wrong before the next shipment is counted.","flaw":"Tavi hides mistakes and tries to solve every problem without asking for help.","internal_conflict":"Tavi wants to protect the Hollow but fears that admitting what the door can do will make everyone else take control of it.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's levy threatens the Hollow's grain stores, and Tavi has little time to find a way to challenge its count.","arc":"Tavi starts out sneaking through yesterday alone and concealing each failed attempt. When a repeated trip through the door leaves Tavi with no time to warn the Hollow Circle about the Cartel's count, Tavi chooses to tell Mira what happened and share the evidence. Tavi ends by facing the levy with help rather than trying to carry the whole burden in secret.","personality_traits":["curious","quick-witted","stubborn","playful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Yesterday's Door","description":"Can open a discovered door onto the same place on the previous day, letting Tavi revisit recent events and notice details missed the first time.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Windmill Listening","description":"Recognizes small changes in the creak and rhythm of the Hollow's windmills, useful for noticing when something has been moved or damaged.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_mira","name":"Mira","role":"supporting","description":"Mira is a young mapmaking student from Silverspine Academy, with neat braids, ink-stained fingertips, and a habit of folding scraps of paper into tiny skybridges. She came to the Hollow to study how its windmills and grain shipments fit into the shifting routes between isles. Mira is Tavi's friend, but she is more comfortable trusting a chart than trusting an unverified story.","motivation":"Make maps that reflect how the archipelago actually works for the people who live on it.","goal":"Chart the Hollow's grain route well enough to show where the Cartel's levy count diverges from the shipments.","flaw":"Mira clings to measurements and established methods even when events do not fit them.","internal_conflict":"She wants her work to matter beyond the Academy, but worries that acting on uncertain information will make her seem careless and undermine her credibility.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel controls the shipping lanes and its levy threatens the Hollow, while the routes Mira needs to chart keep shifting.","arc":"Mira begins by dismissing Tavi's account of the door because it cannot be plotted on her map. When Tavi returns with a detail from yesterday that explains a discrepancy in the grain count, Mira chooses to mark what she witnessed instead of waiting for a perfect chart. She ends willing to use her maps as evidence and to let people, not just measurements, guide her work.","personality_traits":["observant","methodical","earnest","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Shifting-Route Cartography","description":"Charts changing skybridge connections by comparing wind patterns, travelers' reports, and current route markers.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Careful Interviewing","description":"Draws out useful details by asking precise, patient questions.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_ren","name":"Ren","role":"antagonist","description":"Ren is a Drift Cartel tally clerk stationed at Mistral Docks, recognizable by a slate-blue waistcoat, a brass counting charm, and an immaculate stack of shipment ledgers. Ren grew up watching merchants lose cargo when routes changed without warning and believes strict accounting is the only thing keeping trade dependable. Ren treats the Hollow's resistance as a threat to order, not as a plea from neighbors.","motivation":"Keep inter-isle trade predictable and preserve the Cartel's authority over shipping lanes.","goal":"Collect the Hollow's grain levy in full and prevent the tally from being challenged.","flaw":"Ren mistakes obedience to a system for fairness and discounts evidence that does not come through official channels.","internal_conflict":"Ren wants to believe that the Cartel's rules protect ordinary travelers, but knows that a correct ledger can still conceal an unjust demand.","external_conflict":"Tavi and Mira's evidence could disrupt the Cartel's levy and expose weaknesses in Ren's official grain count.","arc":"Ren starts determined to enforce the levy and dismisses Tavi's claims as childish confusion. When Mira's route records and Tavi's account of yesterday reveal that Ren's own tally omitted a shipment, Ren must choose between preserving the appearance of an infallible count and correcting it. Ren ends by acknowledging the error and allowing the Hollow's objection to be heard, though the Cartel's wider conflict with the Wardens remains.","personality_traits":["precise","formal","proud","uneasy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Arithmetic","description":"Tracks cargo counts, tolls, and shipment discrepancies with exceptional precision.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Dockside Negotiation","description":"Uses a calm, official manner to persuade merchants and crews to follow Cartel procedures.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tavi_mira","source_character_id":"chr_tavi","target_character_id":"chr_mira","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tavi trusts Mira's sharp eye, while Mira's careful records help Tavi turn a strange visit to yesterday into evidence against Ren's grain tally."},{"id":"rel_ren_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_ren","target_character_id":"chr_tavi","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ren's effort to enforce the Cartel levy puts Ren directly against Tavi's attempt to protect the Hollow's grain."},{"id":"rel_ren_mira","source_character_id":"chr_ren","target_character_id":"chr_mira","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ren relies on official tallies, while Mira's shifting-route map challenges the count Ren is expected to defend."}]}
