{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_ilyra_vane","name":"Ilyra Vane","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"Ilyra is a young Bridge Warden cartographer raised among Silverspine Academy's shifting charts and the quiet labor that keeps the skybridges intact. Her mother died during a bridge failure blamed on neglected maintenance, leaving Ilyra with a deep distrust of anyone who treats safety as negotiable. She is spare and long-limbed, with wind-chapped cheeks, close-cropped black hair, and a brass measuring compass worn on a cord at her throat. While surveying a rarely used span, she finds an egg lodged in a cloudstone brace; when it hatches, she hides the small, unfamiliar creature rather than report it to either the Wardens or the authorities.","motivation":"Protect lives on the bridges and prove that careful work matters more than tolls or influence.","goal":"Keep the newly hatched creature safe while finding a way to prevent the Cartel from turning it into leverage over the Wardens.","flaw":"She mistakes secrecy and control for responsibility, shutting out people who might help.","internal_conflict":"Ilyra believes that relying on others invites another preventable loss, but protecting the hatchling alone may put it and the bridges in greater danger.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel is pressing the Wardens over rising tolls, and its factor is searching for the hidden creature as a bargaining advantage.","arc":"Ilyra begins convinced that only her vigilance can keep the hatchling safe. When a Cartel search threatens to expose it and strain a vulnerable skybridge, she must choose whether to trust a Hollow Circle miller with the truth and accept help. By the end, she shares responsibility for the creature's safety and uses her knowledge to negotiate protection rather than trying to control every risk herself.","personality_traits":["observant","tenacious","guarded","methodical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge surveying","description":"Reads cable tension, cloudstone wear, and shifting routes to spot dangerous crossings before they fail.","category":"technical"},{"name":"Wind navigation","description":"Uses currents and drifting landmarks to chart safe passages between isles.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_darel_sorn","name":"Darel Sorn","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"Darel Sorn is a Cartel factor at Mistral Docks, where he grew up watching merchants lose cargo and families lose passage when shipping lanes shifted without warning. Now impeccably dressed in salt-dark coats and polished boots, he keeps careful ledgers and remembers every debt. Darel believes the Cartel's control of trade is the only thing preventing another age of stranded isles. When rumors reach him of a rare creature hatched from an egg, he sees a chance to force the Bridge Wardens into a favorable toll agreement, though he intends to keep the creature alive and out of public view.","motivation":"Preserve the Cartel's control of shipping so the isles remain connected and his own authority remains secure.","goal":"Find the hatchling and use its existence to make the Bridge Wardens accept a Cartel-backed settlement to the Toll War.","flaw":"He reduces people and living things to bargaining value, trusting no agreement unless he can make the other side dependent on him.","internal_conflict":"Darel wants to believe his control prevents chaos, yet each attempt to tighten his hold makes the people he claims to protect more willing to resist him.","external_conflict":"The Wardens oppose Cartel tolls, while the Hollow Circle resists grain levies; his search for the hatchling risks uniting both against him.","arc":"Darel begins certain that a secret can be managed like any other cargo. When his pursuit drives Ilyra and the Hollow Circle to cooperate and puts a skybridge crossing at risk, he must choose between seizing the hatchling and accepting a negotiated limit on his leverage. He ends the story forced to reckon with the fact that connection built on coercion can fail as surely as a neglected bridge.","personality_traits":["persuasive","calculating","patient","possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade negotiation","description":"Finds pressure points in contracts and turns competing needs into deals that favor the Cartel.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger memory","description":"Recalls routes, debts, and past agreements with unusual precision.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_renna_mill","name":"Renna Mill","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"Renna Mill is a millwright and grain keeper on The Hollow, part of the quiet network that feeds settlements across the archipelago. Her family endured the Great Calm, and she grew up hearing how shared stores kept neighbors alive when the wind failed. Broad-shouldered, grey-eyed, and usually dusted with flour, Renna keeps a seed pouch tucked into her sleeve and knows which shipments can be delayed without leaving anyone hungry. She encounters Ilyra while carrying supplies along a skybridge and recognizes that the young Warden is hiding more than a maintenance report.","motivation":"Keep food and practical knowledge in the hands of communities that depend on one another.","goal":"Prevent the Cartel's grain levy from making the Hollow Circle dependent on a single shipping authority, while helping Ilyra protect the hatchling.","flaw":"She is so committed to quiet endurance that she waits too long to challenge abuses openly.","internal_conflict":"Renna values patience because it has kept her community alive, but she fears that speaking out will endanger the very people she means to protect.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens the Hollow Circle's stores, and helping Ilyra may give Darel another reason to target the island's shipments.","arc":"Renna starts by believing that keeping her head down is the safest way to preserve the Hollow's stores. When Darel's search threatens both the hatchling and a shipment needed by neighboring isles, she chooses to make the Circle's support visible and share its routes with Ilyra. She ends more willing to confront the Cartel directly, accepting that silence can leave her community isolated.","personality_traits":["practical","steadfast","resourceful","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Repairs windmill mechanisms and adapts them to changing currents.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Stores planning","description":"Calculates how to distribute grain through delays and shortages without exhausting reserves.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_vey","name":"Vey","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","description":"Vey is the small, newly hatched creature Ilyra discovers inside an egg caught in a cloudstone bridge brace near Silverspine Academy. Its dark, slick scales catch faint silver at the edges, and delicate wing membranes tremble whenever a current changes. It has no known place in the archipelago's present-day life, and its first shelter is a padded chart case in Ilyra's rooms. Vey is curious rather than tame: it follows warm air, startles at sudden movement, and responds to the vibration of bridge cables as if they were a language.","motivation":"Find warmth, food, and safety in a world whose sounds and movements are all unfamiliar.","goal":"Stay close to the people and currents that help it survive without being captured or carried away.","flaw":"Its instinct to flee from unfamiliar hands makes it difficult for its protectors to move it safely.","internal_conflict":"Vey seeks closeness and shelter but reacts to care as a threat whenever it feels trapped.","external_conflict":"Darel's search and the danger of exposed skybridges threaten Vey's fragile shelter and its survival.","arc":"Vey begins frightened of every touch and drawn only to the familiar vibration of the bridge. When a Cartel search forces Ilyra to move it across a dangerous span, Vey chooses to remain beside her instead of bolting toward an exposed current. It ends able to accept a small circle of trusted protectors, though it remains wary of the wider world.","personality_traits":["curious","skittish","alert","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Current sense","description":"Detects subtle changes in nearby air currents through its wing membranes.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Cable resonance","description":"Senses vibrations through cloudstone and cable, reacting to strain before it is visible.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilyra_darel","source_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","target_character_id":"chr_darel_sorn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ilyra Vane opposes Darel Sorn's attempt to use the hatchling as leverage in the Cartel's dispute with the Bridge Wardens."},{"id":"rel_darel_ilyra","source_character_id":"chr_darel_sorn","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Darel Sorn sees Ilyra Vane as the Warden obstructing his search and the toll settlement he wants to impose."},{"id":"rel_renna_ilyra","source_character_id":"chr_renna_mill","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Renna Mill offers Ilyra Vane practical aid and a safer route when the Cartel's search threatens the hatchling."},{"id":"rel_ilyra_vey","source_character_id":"chr_ilyra_vane","target_character_id":"chr_vey","relationship_type":"protector","description":"Ilyra Vane shelters Vey after it hatches from the egg and gradually earns its trust."},{"id":"rel_darel_renna","source_character_id":"chr_darel_sorn","target_character_id":"chr_renna_mill","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Darel Sorn's grain levy puts him at odds with Renna Mill, whose work and community depend on the Hollow Circle's stores."}]}
