ill learning its meanings and limits.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Route Reading","description":"Can compare academy charts and wind patterns to identify likely changes in the skybridge network.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_orrin_veyl","name":"Orrin Veyl","role":"supporting","description":"Orrin Veyl is a senior Bridge Warden engineer who helped oversee Nera's initiation at Silverspine Academy. He judged her failure harshly, believing the Wardens could not afford uncertain hands near the skybridges. Years of working with cloudstone cables have left him broad-shouldered, scarred across one palm, and habitually dusted with pale stone fibers. He is exacting in his craft and privately ashamed that his rigid judgment may have driven away the one person capable of interpreting the old language.","motivation":"To keep the skybridge network safe and preserve the Wardens' duty from political control.","goal":"Verify Nera's translation against the bridges themselves and prevent the Cartel from turning it into leverage.","flaw":"He trusts procedure so completely that he can dismiss people whose knowledge does not fit established methods.","internal_conflict":"Orrin wants to protect Nera from dangerous demands but must face that his earlier attempt to protect the Wardens came at the cost of silencing her.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's tolls and demands for access to Nera's knowledge threaten both the bridges and the Wardens' independence.","arc":"Orrin begins certain that only proven engineering methods deserve trust. When Nera's words reveal a clue that ordinary inspection cannot explain, he chooses to stake his reputation on testing her interpretation instead of overruling her. He ends as a more accountable mentor, still demanding evidence but no longer mistaking authority for certainty.","personality_traits":["disciplined","practical","protective","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Can inspect and repair the woven cables that support skybridges.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Structural Judgment","description":"Can recognize strain and likely failure points in bridge structures.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_selka_morn","name":"Selka Morn","role":"antagonist","description":"Selka Morn is a Cartel negotiator based at Mistral Docks, where she built her standing by turning shipping disputes into profitable agreements. She sees herself as a realist: trade lanes and tolls, in her view, keep the archipelago moving and reward those willing to manage risk. Selka dresses in carefully layered travel clothes marked with the Cartel's insignia and carries a ledger of obligations, including wind-debts owed for crossings. She wants Nera's rare knowledge under Cartel control, convinced that a single authority can use it more effectively than divided factions.","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's command of inter-isle trade and prove that centralized control prevents chaos.","goal":"Bring Nera and her translations into the Cartel's custody before the Bridge Wardens can act on them.","flaw":"She treats every relationship as a transaction and assumes that control is the same as security.","internal_conflict":"Selka believes she is protecting the archipelago through order, yet fears that without the Cartel's leverage she has no influence beyond her title.","external_conflict":"The Wardens resist Cartel tolls, and Nera's ability could change how the bridges are understood without the Cartel's permission.","arc":"Selka begins convinced that owning access to knowledge is the surest way to keep trade stable. When her attempt to bargain for Nera's translations deepens the Toll War and alienates useful allies, she must choose between coercion and a negotiated share of risk. She ends less secure in her monopoly, forced to recognize that imposed control can make the instability she claims to prevent.","personality_traits":["persuasive","calculating","composed","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade Negotiation","description":"Can broker shipping agreements and use knowledge of tolls and wind-debts to shape a bargain.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Recall","description":"Keeps close track of obligations, routes, and commercial dependencies across the Cartel's operations.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tavin_reed","name":"Tavin Reed","role":"supporting","description":"Tavin Reed is a miller from The Hollow and a member of the Hollow Circle. He has watched Cartel levies make it harder for farmers to send grain across the skybridges, and he keeps careful records of what his community can spare. Tavin is compact and strong from hauling grain, with sun-faded hair and a flour-dusted apron. He has little patience for academy rivalries, but he is wary of anyone who speaks of sacrifice without sharing its cost.","motivation":"To keep The Hollow's people fed and prevent the grain levy from making their labor serve someone else's profit.","goal":"Help Nera reach the people who can test her knowledge without allowing the Cartel to turn the journey into another toll or debt.","flaw":"His suspicion makes him withhold help until he is sure it cannot be exploited.","internal_conflict":"Tavin wants to defend his community's independence but knows that refusing every outside alliance could leave The Hollow isolated.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens the Hollow Circle, while Nera's struggle with Cartel control may offer a chance to challenge the terms of trade.","arc":"Tavin begins determined to keep The Hollow out of other factions' disputes. When the grain levy makes clear that isolation will not protect the mills, he chooses to share the Circle's records with Nera and the Wardens despite the risk of retaliation. He ends willing to build an alliance while insisting that its costs and benefits be shared openly.","personality_traits":["resourceful","plainspoken","cautious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Can maintain the windmills that grind grain for the archipelago.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Provision Planning","description":"Can estimate stores and organize supplies through careful knowledge of harvests and local needs.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_veyl","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera resents Orrin for treating her failed initiation as proof she could not contribute; his later support is tested by her refusal to accept his judgment without question."},{"id":"rel_orrin_nera","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_veyl","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Orrin once dismissed Nera's abilities, but now tries to guide her safely through the Bridge Wardens' work and must earn her trust."},{"id":"rel_selka_nera","source_character_id":"chr_selka_morn","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Selka wants to control Nera's translations for the Drift Cartel, while Nera seeks to use them without surrendering the knowledge to Cartel authority."},{"id":"rel_tavin_nera","source_character_id":"chr_tavin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavin helps Nera because he believes her work could challenge the Cartel's grain levy, but he insists she respect the Hollow Circle's needs."},{"id":"rel_selka_tavin","source_character_id":"chr_selka_morn","target_character_id":"chr_tavin_reed","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Selka represents the Cartel's grain levy, which Tavin resists on behalf of The Hollow and the Hollow Circle."}]}
