 can make the instability she claims to prevent.","personality_traits":["persuasive","calculating","composed","ambitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade Negotiation","description":"Can broker shipping agreements and use knowledge of tolls and wind-debts to shape a bargain.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Recall","description":"Keeps close track of obligations, routes, and commercial dependencies across the Cartel's operations.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_tavin_reed","name":"Tavin Reed","role":"supporting","description":"Tavin Reed is a miller from The Hollow and a member of the Hollow Circle. He has watched Cartel levies make it harder for farmers to send grain across the skybridges, and he keeps careful records of what his community can spare. Tavin is compact and strong from hauling grain, with sun-faded hair and a flour-dusted apron. He has little patience for academy rivalries, but he is wary of anyone who speaks of sacrifice without sharing its cost.","motivation":"To keep The Hollow's people fed and prevent the grain levy from making their labor serve someone else's profit.","goal":"Help Nera reach the people who can test her knowledge without allowing the Cartel to turn the journey into another toll or debt.","flaw":"His suspicion makes him withhold help until he is sure it cannot be exploited.","internal_conflict":"Tavin wants to defend his community's independence but knows that refusing every outside alliance could leave The Hollow isolated.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy threatens the Hollow Circle, while Nera's struggle with Cartel control may offer a chance to challenge the terms of trade.","arc":"Tavin begins determined to keep The Hollow out of other factions' disputes. When the grain levy makes clear that isolation will not protect the mills, he chooses to share the Circle's records with Nera and the Wardens despite the risk of retaliation. He ends willing to build an alliance while insisting that its costs and benefits be shared openly.","personality_traits":["resourceful","plainspoken","cautious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwrighting","description":"Can maintain the windmills that grind grain for the archipelago.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Provision Planning","description":"Can estimate stores and organize supplies through careful knowledge of harvests and local needs.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_veyl","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera resents Orrin for treating her failed initiation as proof she could not contribute; his later support is tested by her refusal to accept his judgment without question."},{"id":"rel_orrin_nera","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_veyl","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Orrin once dismissed Nera's abilities, but now tries to guide her safely through the Bridge Wardens' work and must earn her trust."},{"id":"rel_selka_nera","source_character_id":"chr_selka_morn","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Selka wants to control Nera's translations for the Drift Cartel, while Nera seeks to use them without surrendering the knowledge to Cartel authority."},{"id":"rel_tavin_nera","source_character_id":"chr_tavin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_nera_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavin helps Nera because he believes her work could challenge the Cartel's grain levy, but he insists she respect the Hollow Circle's needs."},{"id":"rel_selka_tavin","source_character_id":"chr_selka_morn","target_character_id":"chr_tavin_reed","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Selka represents the Cartel's grain levy, which Tavin resists on behalf of The Hollow and the Hollow Circle."}]}
